class:: EnvFollow2
summary:: Half-wave ESP envelope or digital attack/release follower
categories:: UGens>Analysis
related:: Guides/MIRa-MS20-ESP

description::
One normalized envelope in [0,1]. Circuit mode uses a fixed 0.6 V diode approximation, approximately 0.96 ms charging and 22 ms release. Digital mode full-wave rectifies. This class coexists with sc3-plugins EnvFollow.

All parameters except the signal input are construction-time numbers. Outputs are control rate. See the guide for calibration, clipping, latency and model limitations.

classmethods::
method:: kr

argument:: in
Audio input at the calibrated amplified branch.

argument:: inputGain
Fixed gain; one input unit after gain corresponds to one model volt.

argument:: mode
Literal \digital or \circuit.

argument:: attackTime
Digital attack time in seconds; ignored in circuit mode.

argument:: releaseTime
Digital release time in seconds; ignored in circuit mode.

argument:: referenceEnvVolts
Positive fixed envelope reference, default 5 model volts.

returns::
One normalized envelope in [0,1]. Circuit mode uses a fixed 0.6 V diode approximation, approximately 0.96 ms charging and 22 ms release. Digital mode full-wave rectifies. This class coexists with sc3-plugins EnvFollow.

examples::
code::
{ EnvFollow2.kr(SinOsc.ar(220, 0, 4)).poll; Silent.ar(2) }.play;
::
